1
00:00:00,066 --> 00:00:03,366
You should be concerned about NextEra's takeover of Virginia's Dominion Energy.

2
00:00:03,366 --> 00:00:08,033
This is part one, explaining exactly why, starting with political corruption. First,

3
00:00:08,033 --> 00:00:13,066
Virginia is only one of four states that allow unlimited corporate political contributions,

4
00:00:13,166 --> 00:00:15,366
and Dominion is already abusing that.

5
00:00:15,366 --> 00:00:18,366
It gave $3.67 million in just one quarter,

6
00:00:18,366 --> 00:00:22,333
and more than half of its political giving this year came after the merger was announced.

7
00:00:22,333 --> 00:00:24,700
The NextEra takeover would make it even worse.

8
00:00:24,700 --> 00:00:28,033
NextEra spent over $125 million on politics that we know about,

9
00:00:28,033 --> 00:00:31,700
and it just won one of the largest rate hikes in U.S. history in Florida.

10
00:00:31,700 --> 00:00:34,900
It also has a long history of shady political dealings:

11
00:00:34,900 --> 00:00:39,400
a ghost-candidate scheme that ended in a state senator's felony conviction,

12
00:00:39,433 --> 00:00:46,400
a fake news outlet, a nearly $250,000 job offer to a city council member on the condition that they resign,

13
00:00:46,533 --> 00:00:50,200
and a $150 million settlement that a federal judge threw out.

14
00:00:50,200 --> 00:00:53,466
If you're worried about this deal, your lawmakers need to hear from you.

15
00:00:53,466 --> 00:00:56,000
Contact them today and share your concerns.

16
00:00:56,033 --> 00:00:58,300
Ask them what they're doing to protect their constituents,

17
00:00:58,300 --> 00:01:01,600
and urge them to come out publicly in opposition to the acquisition

18
00:01:01,600 --> 00:01:03,533
and in support of Virginia's democracy.
